2024-08-03 09:20:09,082 - INFO - Updated journal_filename session:1wxxhVjSo6w: [{'result': [{'category': 'Insights', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'In 2021, Raja et al. published ‘The Markov Blanket Trick’, which argued that “the FEP [Free Energy Principle] is not the general principle it is claimed to be, and that active inference is not the all-encompassing process theory it is purported to be either.” This led to a flurry of responses from within the active inference community, with commentaries published by Friston, Ramstead and Albarracin & Pitliya, amongst others. In this episode of Active Inference Insights, we unpick this controversial paper with the help of its primary author, Vicente Raja, and Jeff Beck, a computational neuroscientist studying probabilistic reasoning in humans and animals. \n\nVicente Raja\nhttps://www.rotman.uwo.ca/portfolio-items/raja-vicente/\nhttps://twitter.com/DioVicen\n\nJeff Beck\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/jeff-beck-6b5085196\n\nDarius Parvizi-Wayne\nhttps://twitter.com/dparviziwayne\n\nActive Inference Insititute\nhttps://www.activeinference.org\nhttps://twitter.com/InferenceActive', 'filename': 'youtube_1wxxhVjSo6w.mp4', 'id': 'session:1wxxhVjSo6w', 'journal_filename': 'Insights_007_youtube_1wxxhVjSo6w.simple.txt', 'published_at': '2024-01-11T16:00:09Z', 'series': 'Insights_007', 'session_name': '1wxxhVjSo6w', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1wxxhVjSo6w/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'Vicente Raja & Jeff Beck  ~ Active Inference Insights 007 ~ The Markov Blanket Trick Debate', 'transcribed': True, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1wxxhVjSo6w', 'wav_extracted': True}], 'status': 'OK', 'time': '3.931575ms'}]
