2024-08-03 13:49:35,666 - INFO - Updated journal_filename session:RpOrRw4EhTo: [{'result': [{'category': 'Courses/PhysicsAsInformationProcessing_ChrisFields', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'Course materials \nhttps://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/fields-physics-2023\n\nMore information\nhttps://www.activeinference.org/education/Physics-Fields-2023\n\n“Physics as Information Processing”\nCourse taught by Chris Fields\nCourse assistant is Ander Aguirre\nHosted during 2023 by the Active Inference Institute\n\nSession 1 (18 May) will review some history, starting with Boltzmann’s relation between entropy and energy, and continuing through Church’s and Turing’s models of computation, Shannon’s information theory, the “black box” methods of Ashby et al., Pearl’s definition of a Markov blanket, Bekenstein’s area law for black holes, ‘t Hooft’s and Susskind’s formulation of the holographic principle, the ideas of objects, interfaces, and virtual machines in computing, up to Friston’s 2010 and 2013 papers introducing active inference. The goal of this session is to establish the idea of a Markov blanket as a communication interface.\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.org/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.gg/8VNKNp4jtx \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams', 'filename': 'youtube_RpOrRw4EhTo.mp4', 'id': 'session:RpOrRw4EhTo', 'journal_filename': 'Lecture_1_youtube_RpOrRw4EhTo.simple.txt', 'published_at': '2023-05-19T04:02:30Z', 'series': 'Lecture_1', 'session_name': 'RpOrRw4EhTo', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RpOrRw4EhTo/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': '"Physics as Information Processing" ~ Chris Fields ~ Lecture 1', 'transcribed': True, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RpOrRw4EhTo', 'wav_extracted': True}], 'status': 'OK', 'time': '6.52216ms'}]
