2025-09-30 17:46:25,368 - INFO - Updated session in database: [{'category': 'GuestStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'From Contextuality to Social Constraints - An Active Inference ontology for participatory realism and social change\n\nAuthor : Avel GUÉNIN—CARLUT\n\nAbstract : Unlike physical systems constituted of inert matter, biological and cognitive systems are characterized by their ability for adaptive regulation, powered by (and dual to) an active process of making sense of their world. We consider the physical basis of this phenomena through the notion of contextuality, the property of physical systems (such as quantum particles) whose states are irreducibly brought about (rather than revealed) by the very act of their observation. We further consider the relevance of Active Inference to account for cognitive contextuality, and the formal limitation related to its mathematical grounding in the Free Energy Principle. Furthermore, we analyze the special case of agents (such as humans) who are prone to reflexively consider their own beliefs and actions as communicative acts, a cognitive attitude we call the existential stance. We argue that this property (given the contextual / predictive nature of cognition) entails a profound embedding of the human mind in its social and material context. We formalize the notion of social constraints, a novel ontology of cognitive and social organization which reconciles the structuration of human cognitive by culture and the evolution of culture by human agency.\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://www.activeinference.institute/\nActivities: https://activities.activeinference.institute/ \nDiscord: https://discord.activeinference.institute/\nDonate: http://donate.activeinference.institute/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nX: https://x.com/InferenceActive \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://video.activeinference.institute/', 'episode': '1', 'filename': 'NZnlrI-6mS8.wav', 'from_coda_json': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Avel Guénin-Carlut', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=6bymihfd5fcfi6nccjes), 'is_private': False, 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman', 'paper_link': '', 'published_at': '2025-03-10T03:24:09Z', 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2025, 3, 9, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'GuestStream_099', 'session_name': 'NZnlrI-6mS8', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NZnlrI-6mS8/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf GuestStream 099.1 ~ Avel Guénin-Carlut: "From Contextuality to Social Constraints"', 'transcribed': False, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NZnlrI-6mS8', 'wav_extracted': True}]
