2025-09-30 19:09:38,872 - INFO - Updated session in database: [{'category': 'GuestStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'Benjamin Nelson\n"Decoding the ARC: The Evolution of Reason in the Abstract Reasoning Corpus"\nhttps://linktr.ee/borrowedladder\nhttps://github.com/Infrabenji/ARCANGEL-X-LEGION\nhttps://zenodo.org/records/14907843? "From ARC test to Archetype: ARCANGEL EP and the Emergence of the State Managed System"\n\nOn October 28th, 2024, ARCANGEL shattered the theoretical maxim of the Abstract Reasoning Corpus (ARC). Then on February 5th, 2025, ARCANGEL EP achieved what many considered impossible: perfect scores on the ARC’s public and semi-private evaluation. Completing all 800 challenges in just over 4 hours, ARCANGEL stands unrivaled. True to Chollet’s vision in "On the Measure of Intelligence", ARCANGEL solved every problem without pre-training, propagation, prior knowledge of the challenges, and without exposure to the training and evaluation sets prior to testing. ARCANGEL accomplished this technological feat leveraging only a single 2.3 GHz Dual-Core Intel Core i5 with 8GB of RAM and wall power. The advancements contained within ARCANGEL’s framework represent a shifting paradigm, evidence of an unexplored frontier in the development of artificial intelligence, the State-Managed System. At its core is the pioneering work of Dr. Robert Worden, whose formulation of the requirement for cognition represents one of the most significant breakthroughs in scientific history. Derived from Active Inference and the Free Energy Principle, the State Managed System mirrors biological cognition through representational components known as cognitive mechanisms. From this architecture a hyper-intelligent system emerges, unparalleled in self-sufficient learning, abstract reasoning, problem-solving, and decision-making. ARCANGEL redefines the very measure of intelligence, establishing an unprecedented benchmark that fundamentally surpasses the capabilities of existing distributed systems.\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://www.activeinference.institute/\nActivities: https://activities.activeinference.institute/ \nDiscord: https://discord.activeinference.institute/\nDonate: http://donate.activeinference.institute/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nX: https://x.com/InferenceActive \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://video.activeinference.institute/', 'episode': '2', 'filename': 'E3vyVxMZanA.wav', 'from_coda_json': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Benjamin Nelson', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=93n0ub0gcr2wz9rmd2oz), 'is_private': False, 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman', 'paper_link': '', 'published_at': '2025-02-22T23:35:10Z', 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2025, 2, 21, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'GuestStream_090', 'session_name': 'E3vyVxMZanA', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/E3vyVxMZanA/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf GuestStream 090.2 Decoding the ARC: The Evolution of Reason in the Abstract Reasoning Corpus', 'transcribed': False, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E3vyVxMZanA', 'wav_extracted': True}]
