lve the ambiguity of both environments by appropriately contextualizing their observations based on prediction accuracy only. In addition, they infer optimal policies flexibly for any target observation in the environment.\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.institute/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.activeinference.institute/ \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams', 'episode': '1', 'filename': '1Qr7um2W-Rc.wav', 'from_coda_json': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Joséphine Pazem', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=tb68jfehce1agvfu22dz), 'is_private': False, 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman,Alexander Vining,Hans Brigel,Lukas Fiderer,Marius Krumm', 'paper_link': '', 'published_at': '2024-12-18T05:39:13Z', 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2024, 12, 17, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'GuestStream_094', 'session_name': '1Qr7um2W-Rc', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1Qr7um2W-Rc/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf GuestStream 094.1 ~ Joséphine Pazem:, "Free Energy Projective Simulation (FEPS)"', 'transcribed': True, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Qr7um2W-Rc', 'wav_extracted': True}]
