2025-10-01 12:52:05,392 - INFO - Updated session in database: [{'category': 'GuestStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'Computers, Meaning and Consciousness\nRobert Worden \n\nThis talk uses simple arguments to derive a negative result: that a computer cannot be conscious. If the brain is only a neural computer, brains cannot be conscious. All information in a running computer is encoded; without decoding, it is not about any defined external thing. So a computer cannot support consciousness of external things.\n\nTo support consciousness, brains must contain something else besides neural computation. That something could be an analogue model of 3-D space. Analogue models contain information which requires no decoding, and which could be experienced in consciousness.\n\nhttps://wave-hypothesis.activeinference.institute/\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://www.activeinference.institute/\nActivities: https://activities.activeinference.institute/ \nDiscord: https://discord.activeinference.institute/\nDonate: http://donate.activeinference.institute/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nX: https://x.com/InferenceActive \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://video.activeinference.institute/', 'episode': '5', 'filename': 'p7iq4AAIwjc.wav', 'from_coda_json': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Robert Worden', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=vr9dz7zr554sbk1lgkae), 'is_private': False, 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman,David Rudrauf,Kenneth Williford,Karl J Friston,Benjamin Nelson,Brianna O’Keefe,Giulio Corsi', 'paper_link': '', 'published_at': '2025-04-15T03:01:33Z', 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2025, 4, 14, 7, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'GuestStream_082', 'session_name': 'p7iq4AAIwjc', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/p7iq4AAIwjc/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf GuestStream 082.5 ~ Robert Worden "Computers, Meaning and Consciousness"', '