2025-10-01 15:16:01,765 - INFO - Updated session in database: [{'category': 'ArtStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': '"Literature as Uncertainty Practice – Creative Encounters with the World"\nKarin Kukkonen\n\nWith: Bruno Viandrola (Kiel) and Federico Pianzola (Groningen)\n\nEnvironments are more and more perceived as volatile. A world in crisis is not stable enough for us to\nlearn from prediction errors and devise new, reliable protocols to deal with the unexpected (see\nMiller et al. 2023). Literature, however, continually plunges its readers into such volatile\nenvironments, by providing a designed sensory flow or «probability design» (Kukkonen 2020). In this\ntalk, I will discuss how the form or composition in a narrative guides readers’ attention through\ncontingent events, while keeping them immersed at the same time.\nI will then develop suggestions for how the experimentation and play of literary narratives shapes\nvolatile designer environments that invite and enable creative encounters with the world.\n\nFurther reading:\nKukkonen, Karin (2023). «Literature as Uncertainty Practice: An Anomaly at the End of Literature»\nDVJS 97: 1143-1152. https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41245-023-00219-4\nKukkonen, Karin (2024). «Contingency Traps: The Role of Form in Creative Processes.» Neohelicon\n51: 105-116. https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11059-024-00741-0\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.org/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.gg/8VNKNp4jtx \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams', 'episode': 1, 'filename': 'x6rwST67ugU.wav', 'from_coda_csv': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Karin Kukkonen', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=2kl1mbycd4fa4m3rzvhg), 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman', 'published_at': datetime.datet