2025-10-02 02:15:38,900 - INFO - Updated session in database: [{'category': 'Insights', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'Active Inference Insights 013 is all about modelling: not only how we model our lived world, but also how we might scientifically model that modelling process ourselves. With neuro-computationalist Ryan Smith at the helm, expect to learn about the difference between empirical computational psychiatry and in-silico simulations, the role of aberrant precision-weighting in neuropsychological disorders and how a little parameter called ‘gamma’ might hold the key to a life of wellbeing.\n\nRyan Smith\nhttps://www.laureateinstitute.org/ryan-smith.html\nhttps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ScOne9wAAAAJ&hl=en\n\nDarius Parvizi-Wayne\nhttps://twitter.com/dparviziwayne\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/profile/Darius-Parvizi-Wayne\n\nActive Inference Insititute\nhttps://www.activeinference.org\nhttps://twitter.com/InferenceActive', 'episode': None, 'filename': 'bQAJKi5ewDI.wav', 'from_coda_csv': True, 'github': '', 'guests': 'Ryan Smith', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=y5nnuctbjztasmspn1h0), 'other_participants': 'Darius Parvizi-Wayne', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2024, 2, 29, 16, 0, 7, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2024, 2, 29, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'Insights_013', 'session_name': 'bQAJKi5ewDI', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bQAJKi5ewDI/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'Ryan Smith ~ Active Inference Insights 013 ~ Wellbeing, Modelling, Precision', 'transcribed': False, 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bQAJKi5ewDI', 'wav_extracted': True}]
