2025-10-13 15:59:52,140 - INFO - Copied MUaKYWKs0kk.simple.txt to /mnt/md0/projects/ActiveInferenceJournal/ModelStream/ModelStream_013/Metadata/ModelStream_013.1_MUaKYWKs0kk.simple.txt
2025-10-13 15:59:52,144 - INFO - Updated metadata_filename and github URL for session:rzk8ppeai7m4ap7911td: [{'category': 'ModelStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': "Synthesizing the Born rule with reinforcement learning\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19011\nRodrigo S. Piera, John B. DeBrota, Matthew B. Weiss, Gabriela B. Lemos, Jailson Sales Araújo, Gabriel H. Aguilar, Jacques L. Pienaar\n\nAccording to the subjective Bayesian interpretation of quantum theory (QBism), quantum mechanics is a tool that an agent would be wise to use when making bets about natural phenomena. In particular, the Born rule is understood to be a decision-making norm, an ideal which one should strive to meet even if usually falling short in practice. What is required for an agent to make decisions that conform to quantum mechanics? Here we investigate how a realistic (hence non-ideal) agent might deviate from the Born rule in its decisions. To do so we simulate a simple agent as a reinforcement-learning algorithm that makes `bets' on the outputs of a symmetric informationally-complete measurement (SIC) and adjusts its decisions in order to maximize its expected return. We quantify how far the algorithm's decision-making behavior departs from the ideal form of the Born rule and investigate the limiting factors. We propose an experimental implementation of the scenario using heralded single photons.\n\n[Submitted on 29 Apr 2024 (v1), last revised 5 Aug 2024 (this version, v2)]\n\n----\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.org/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.gg/8VNKNp4jtx \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams", 'episode': '1', 'filename': 'MUaKYWKs0kk.wav', 'from_coda_csv': True, 'github': 'https://github.com/ActiveInferenceInstitute/ActiveInferenceJournal/tree/main/ModelStream/ModelStream_013', 'guests': 'Jacques Pienaar', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=rzk8ppeai7m4ap7911td), 'metadata_filename': 'ModelStream_013.1_MUaKYWKs0kk.simple.txt', 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman,Ander Aguirre', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2024, 8, 24, 8, 44, 36, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2024, 8, 23, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'ModelStream_013', 'session_name': 'MUaKYWKs0kk', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MUaKYWKs0kk/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf ModelStream 013.1 ~ "Synthesizing the Born rule with reinforcement learning" Jacques Pienaar', 'transcribed': True, 'transcript_method': 'WhisperX', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MUaKYWKs0kk', 'wav_extracted': True}]
