2025-10-18 15:30:57,210 - INFO - Updated metadata_filename and github URL for session:z71lk5puwytuqyqbfg32: [{'category': 'GuestStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': 'Raphael Milliere, Charles Rathkopf\n"Anthropocentric bias and the possibility of artificial cognition"\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2407.03859\n\nEvaluating the cognitive capacities of large language models (LLMs) requires overcoming not only anthropomorphic but also anthropocentric biases. This article identifies two types of anthropocentric bias that have been neglected: overlooking how auxiliary factors can impede LLM performance despite competence (Type-I), and dismissing LLM mechanistic strategies that differ from those of humans as not genuinely competent (Type-II). Mitigating these biases necessitates an empirically-driven, iterative approach to mapping cognitive tasks to LLM-specific capacities and mechanisms, which can be done by supplementing carefully designed behavioral experiments with mechanistic studies.\n\narXiv:2407.03859\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.org/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.gg/8VNKNp4jtx \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams', 'episode': '1', 'filename': 'Wn65WcYGQSA.wav', 'from_coda_csv': True, 'github': 'https://github.com/ActiveInferenceInstitute/ActiveInferenceJournal/tree/main/GuestStream/GuestStream_084', 'guests': 'Raphael Milliere,Charles Rathkopf', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=z71lk5puwytuqyqbfg32), 'metadata_filename': 'GuestStream_084.1_Wn65WcYGQSA.simple.txt', 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2024, 7, 23, 0, 40, 4, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2024, 7, 22, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'GuestStream_084', 'session_name': 'Wn65WcYGQSA', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Wn65WcYGQSA/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf GuestStream 084.1 ~ Anthropocentric bias and the possibility of artificial cognition', 'transcribed': True, 'transcript_method': 'WhisperX', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wn65WcYGQSA', 'wav_extracted': True}]
