2025-10-18 15:54:13,828 - INFO - Updated metadata_filename and github URL for session:lja3thk9fzelqkmw4u3g: [{'category': 'MathStream', 'channel_title': 'Active Inference Institute', 'description': '"Constructor Theory as Process Theory"\nhttps://act2023.github.io/papers/paper27.pdf\nStefano Gogioso, Vincent Wang-Mascianica, Muhammad Hamza Waseem, Carlo Maria Scandolo, Bob Coecke\n\nConstructor theory is a meta-theoretic approach that seeks to characterise concrete theories of physics in terms of the (im)possibility to implement certain abstract “tasks” by means of physical processes. Process theory, on the other hand, pursues analogous characterisation goals in terms of the compositional structure of said processes, concretely presented through the lens of (symmetric monoidal) category theory. In this work, we show how to formulate fundamental notions of constructor theory within the canvas of process theory. Specifically, we exploit the functorial interplay between the symmetric monoidal structure of the category of sets and relations, where the abstract tasks live, and that of symmetric monoidal categories from physics, where concrete processes can be found to implement said tasks. Through this, we answer the question of how constructor theory relates to the broader body of process-theoretic literature, and provide the impetus for future collaborative work between the fields.\n\nActive Inference Institute information: \nWebsite: https://activeinference.org/ \nTwitter: https://twitter.com/InferenceActive \nDiscord: https://discord.gg/8VNKNp4jtx \nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/ActiveInference/ \nActive Inference Livestreams: https://coda.io/@active-inference-institute/livestreams', 'episode': '1', 'filename': 'kJUVdt-fN7U.wav', 'from_coda_csv': True, 'github': 'https://github.com/ActiveInferenceInstitute/ActiveInferenceJournal/tree/main/MathStream/MathStream_007', 'guests': 'Vincent Wang-Mascianica', 'id': RecordID(table_name=session, record_id=lja3thk9fzelqkmw4u3g), 'metadata_filename': 'MathStream_007.1_kJUVdt-fN7U.simple.txt', 'other_participants': 'Daniel Friedman,Muhammad Hamza Waseem', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2023, 9, 20, 3, 46, 29, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'scheduled_date': datetime.datetime(2023, 9, 19, 8, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'series': 'MathStream_007', 'session_name': 'kJUVdt-fN7U', 'slides_url': '', 'thumbnails': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kJUVdt-fN7U/mqdefault.jpg', 'title': 'ActInf MathStream 007.1 ~ "Constructor Theory as Process Theory", Vincent Wang-Mascianica et al.', 'transcribed': True, 'transcript_method': 'WhisperX', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kJUVdt-fN7U', 'wav_extracted': True}]
